  "text": "2:41¢ all §¥ @e\n\n& re eee xx\nthings to remember:\n* the human-animal bond is mutually\nbeneficial: both parties release oxytocin during\npositive contact.\n* turning back in a cat signals trust. the\nchecking glance signals safety. both are\nexpressions of genuine attachment.\n* dogs and cats signal bonding differently:\napplying dog-bond signals to a cat produces a\nfalse negative almost every time.\n* the most reliable cross-species signal: when\nstressed, a bonded animal looks for you\nspecifically.\n",
